```c
c->x86_cache_mbm_width_offset = eax & 0xff;
if (c->x86_vendor == X86_VENDOR_AMD && !c->x86_cache_mbm_width_offset)
    c->x86_cache_mbm_width_offset = MBM_CNTR_WIDTH_OFFSET_AMD;
```
Reason:
The fix modifies the logic to set the MBM counter width for AMD processors to a predefined offset (44 bits) if the width is not already set. This adjustment allows the software to accurately measure higher bandwidths without overflow, thus resolving the issue with the previous hardcoded 24-bit width.

